{"id": "EUVD-2026-75300", "enisaUuid": "98566b10-92ba-306d-b9d1-20e63cf3f79c", "description": "fs_read_glyphs() in the libXfont2 font-server client (src/fc/fserve.c) indexes the per-character encoding[] array using num_chars from the FS_QueryXBitmaps16 reply, but that array was allocated with a size derived from num_extents in the separate FS_QueryXExtents16 reply. The two CARD32 fields are never cross-checked.\nA malicious or compromised font server can send a small num_extents (e.g. 1) in the extents reply, then a large num_chars (e.g. 100000) in the bitmaps reply. This causes attacker-controlled out-of-bounds heap read and writes.", "datePublished": "2026-09-10T08:15:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-10T12:45:33", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://bugzilla.suse.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2026-59679"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-59679", "GHSA-g44m-wpf7-gr7x"], "assigner": "suse", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a50b7d9-2d18-3f40-891f-86518e55db52", "product": {"name": "Image SLES15-SP6-SAP", "vendor": {"name": "SUSE"}}, "product_version": "? <2.0.3-150000.3.6.1"}, {"id": "0b644b4a-b421-31a3-a688-df8fe6ee5a0a", "product": {"name": "Image SLES15-SP6-SAP-Hardened-BYOS", "vendor": {"name": "SUSE"}}, "product_version": "? <2.0.3-150000.3.6.1"}, {"id": "0ba24f26-51c4-39df-a15a-d3bdd71c2fd3", "product": {"name": "Image SLES15-SP6-SAP-BYOS-Azure", "vendor": {"name": "SUSE"}}, "product_version": "? <2.0.3-150000.3.6.1"}, {"id": "0bc083c3-b4a1-396c-839b-3b4acd95a475", "product": {"name": "Image SLES15-SP6-SAP-Hardened-EC2", "vendor": {"name": "SUSE"}}, "product_version": "? <2.0.3-150000.3.6.1"}, {"id": "0ddc32ab-208a-3953-8af0-0133619169b4", "product": {"name": "Image SLES15-SP7-SAP-Hardened-BYOS-EC2", "vendor": {"name": "SUSE"}}, "product_version": "? <2.0.3-150000.3.6.1"}, {"id": "1320bd28-6ff3-3a25-83a2-8b06c02fce15", "product": {"name": "Image SLES15-SP